<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Austerlitz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1805</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Battle of the Three Emperors · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-third-coalition">War of the Third Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Austerlitz was fought on 2 December 1805 near Austerlitz (Slavkov u Brna) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-third-coalition">War of the Third Coalition</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s French army decisively defeated the Russian and Austrian armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Alexander I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Emperor Francis II</a>. The victory forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> to accept the Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Pressburg</a>, led to the dissolution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, and is often counted as Napoleon's greatest triumph.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-austerlitz.jpg" alt="Battle of Austerlitz" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François Gérard · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_bataille_d%27Austerlitz._2_decembre_1805_(Fran%C3%A7ois_G%C3%A9rard).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
